FileSystemEnumerable allows us to traverse a directory in various ways. As you can see,
we can filter certain files and file types by using a combination of EnumerationOptions
and ShouldIncludePredicate. Once we have our list, we can simply iterate it as we
would any collection; in our case, we're calling the method that we passed in and passing
back the filename.
