Installing the Windows Service
The installation of a Windows Service, especially for .NET Core (at least at the time of
writing), is a very manual process. Furthermore, because we are using a configuration file,
we'll need to make some slight tweaks so that the service will know where to look for the
config file.
Code changes
When we install the service, we'll need to tell it where to look for the config file. We can do
that by simply passing the parameter into the service. There are actually two ways to do
this; the first (and the one that we're interested in) is to pass the parameter in during the
installation of the service. This gets passed into the Main method. The second is passed in
via the service management utility; the arguments are passed into the OnStart method of
the service.
In our case, we're interested in changing the Main method:
